                            **USER management**

**Types of users in linux:
1. Root user:
--> root user is a super user in system, who has all access pass to the system functionality.

2. Standard user:
--> standrd users are those users which are created by root user. 
-they have limited permissions compared to the root user.

3. system user:
--> system users are the users account created by the system rather than root user
who used to run background processes and services

